{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0438","billNumberShort":"H.B. 438","billNumberLong":"HB0438S05","fileNumber":"2026FL0366","shortTitle":"Artificial Intelligence Amendments","currentSubVersion":"5","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"FIEFID","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Fiefia, Doug","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"CULLIKA","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Cullimore, Kirk A.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill enacts the Companion Chatbot Safety Act to regulate operators of companion chatbots and protect consumers.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms; <hr><ltbullet>requires operators of companion chatbots to comply with the Utah Consumer Privacy Act; <hr><ltbullet>establishes disclosure and data protection requirements for operators; <hr><ltbullet>establishes additional safety requirements for operators serving minor users; <hr><ltbullet>authorizes rulemaking for age assurance standards; <hr><ltbullet>requires annual reporting by operators to the Office of Artificial Intelligence Policy; <hr><ltbullet>grants enforcement authority to the Division of Consumer Protection; <hr><ltbullet>provides for administrative fines and civil penalties; <hr><ltbullet>establishes a safe harbor provision for operators; <hr><ltbullet>requires the Office of Artificial Intelligence Policy to study and report on companion chatbot safety standards; and <hr><ltbullet>provides a severability clause.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Scott Elder","fiscalAnalyst":"Steven M. Allred","lastAction":"House/ filed","lastActionOwner":"House file for bills not passed","lastActionDate":"3/6/2026","trackingID":"LJJJGOPQNU","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 11:18:44.797","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"desc